{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And it went out</b> — from the arrangement of other angels, and behold, another goes out after the one that went out first, and it is the curse. Now he turns to rebuke those who remained in Babylon and did not come to build the House and to dwell in the Holy Land, to fulfill the commandments of HaShem, for it is the beginning of the visions of the horns, the building of Jerusalem, and also after the visions of the glory of HaShem that He commanded to perform for those who come from the exile, the volunteers. And behold, in the first vision he saw a scroll, and now he does not know what it is, for the curse appears to one in whose hand theft is found, or to one who knows he has sworn falsely, and this one that goes out is hidden and concealed in the heart."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:02.841506905Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}